---@field userId string A stable, unique identifier for the end user. The `userId` must be unique across all end users in the developer's CDP Project. It must be between 1 and 100 characters long and can only contain alphanumeric characters and hyphens.
---@field authenticationMethods coinbase.AuthenticationMethods
---@field mfaMethods? coinbase.MFAMethods
---@field evmAccounts coinbase.EndUserEvmAccountsList **DEPRECATED**: Use `evmAccountObjects` instead for richer account information. The list of EVM account addresses associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 EVM accounts.
---@field evmAccountObjects coinbase.EndUserEvmAccountObjectsList The list of EVM accounts associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 EVM accounts.
---@field evmSmartAccounts coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccountsList **DEPRECATED**: Use `evmSmartAccountObjects` instead for richer account information including owner relationships. The list of EVM smart account addresses associated with the end user. Each EVM EOA can own one smart account.
---@field evmSmartAccountObjects coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccountObjectsList The list of EVM smart accounts associated with the end user. Each EVM EOA can own one smart account.
---@field solanaAccounts coinbase.EndUserSolanaAccountsList **DEPRECATED**: Use `solanaAccountObjects` instead for richer account information. The list of Solana account addresses associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 Solana accounts.
---@field solanaAccountObjects coinbase.EndUserSolanaAccountObjectsList The list of Solana accounts associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 Solana accounts.
---@field createdAt string The date and time when the end user was created, in ISO 8601 format.

---Information about an EVM account associated with an end user.
---@class coinbase.EndUserEvmAccount
---@field address string The address of the EVM account.
---@field createdAt string The date and time when the account was created, in ISO 8601 format.
---@field exportedAt? string|distilled.Null The date and time when the account's private key was first exported, in ISO 8601 format. This is set on the first export and preserved on subsequent exports; it is not updated on re-export.
---@field ejectedAt? string|distilled.Null The date and time when the account's key was ejected (marked for deletion), in ISO 8601 format. Populated when the account has been ejected. The account record remains queryable after this timestamp is set; it reflects when ejection was requested, not when the key material is purged.

---The list of EVM accounts associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 EVM accounts.
---@alias coinbase.EndUserEvmAccountObjectsList coinbase.EndUserEvmAccount[]

---**DEPRECATED**: Use `evmAccountObjects` instead for richer account information. The list of EVM account addresses associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 EVM accounts.
---@alias coinbase.EndUserEvmAccountsList string[]

---Information about an EVM smart account associated with an end user.
---@class coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccount
---@field address string The address of the EVM smart account.
---@field ownerAddresses coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccountOwnerAddressesList The addresses of the EVM EOA accounts that own this smart account. Smart accounts can have multiple owners, such as when spend permissions are enabled.
---@field createdAt string The date and time when the account was created, in ISO 8601 format.

---The list of EVM smart accounts associated with the end user. Each EVM EOA can own one smart account.
---@alias coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccountObjectsList coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccount[]

---The addresses of the EVM EOA accounts that own this smart account. Smart accounts can have multiple owners, such as when spend permissions are enabled.
---@alias coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccountOwnerAddressesList string[]

---**DEPRECATED**: Use `evmSmartAccountObjects` instead for richer account information including owner relationships. The list of EVM smart account addresses associated with the end user. Each EVM EOA can own one smart account.
---@alias coinbase.EndUserEvmSmartAccountsList string[]

---Information about a Solana account associated with an end user.
---@class coinbase.EndUserSolanaAccount
---@field address string The base58 encoded address of the Solana account.
---@field createdAt string The date and time when the account was created, in ISO 8601 format.
---@field exportedAt? string|distilled.Null The date and time when the account's private key was first exported, in ISO 8601 format. This is set on the first export and preserved on subsequent exports; it is not updated on re-export.
---@field ejectedAt? string|distilled.Null The date and time when the account's key was ejected (marked for deletion), in ISO 8601 format. Populated when the account has been ejected. The account record remains queryable after this timestamp is set; it reflects when ejection was requested, not when the key material is purged.

---The list of Solana accounts associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 Solana accounts.
---@alias coinbase.EndUserSolanaAccountObjectsList coinbase.EndUserSolanaAccount[]

---**DEPRECATED**: Use `solanaAccountObjects` instead for richer account information. The list of Solana account addresses associated with the end user. End users can have up to 10 Solana accounts.
---@alias coinbase.EndUserSolanaAccountsList string[]

---The result of a vault fee redemption from an EVM account after broadcast.
---@class coinbase.EoaVaultRedeemFeesResponse
---@field transactionHash string The hash of the broadcast fee redemption transaction, as a 0x-prefixed hex string.

---An ERC-20 approval transaction payload. The payer must send `data` as an EVM transaction via `eth_sendTransaction` and return the resulting transaction hash.
