_added"|"health.status.updated"|"health.maintenance.scheduled"|"health.maintenance.started"|"health.maintenance.completed"|"health.maintenance.canceled"|"customers.capability.changed"|"customers.customer.deleted"|"customers.requirement.changed"

---@class coinbase.EvmAccount
---@field address string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address.
---@field name? string An optional name for the account. Account names can consist of alphanumeric characters and hyphens, and be between 2 and 36 characters long. Account names are guaranteed to be unique across all EVM accounts in the developer's CDP Project.
---@field policies? coinbase.EvmAccountPoliciesList The list of policy IDs that apply to the account. This will include both the project-level policy and the account-level policy, if one exists.
---@field createdAt? string The UTC ISO 8601 timestamp at which the account was created.
---@field updatedAt? string The UTC ISO 8601 timestamp at which the account was last updated.

---The list of policy IDs that apply to the account. This will include both the project-level policy and the account-level policy, if one exists.
---@alias coinbase.EvmAccountPoliciesList string[]

---A schema for specifying a criterion for the `to` field of an EVM transaction.
---@class coinbase.EvmAddressCriterion
---@field type coinbase.EvmAddressCriterionType|string The type of criterion to use. This should be `evmAddress`.
---@field addresses coinbase.EvmAddressCriterionAddressesList A list of 0x-prefixed EVM addresses that the transaction's `to` field should be compared to. There is a limit of 300 addresses per criterion.
---@field operator coinbase.EvmAddressCriterionOperator|string The operator to use for the comparison. The transaction's `to` field will be on the left-hand side of the operator, and the `addresses` field will be on the right-hand side.

---A list of 0x-prefixed EVM addresses that the transaction's `to` field should be compared to. There is a limit of 300 addresses per criterion.
---@alias coinbase.EvmAddressCriterionAddressesList string[]

---The operator to use for the comparison. The transaction's `to` field will be on the left-hand side of the operator, and the `addresses` field will be on the right-hand side.
---@alias coinbase.EvmAddressCriterionOperator "in"|"not in"

---The type of criterion to use. This should be `evmAddress`.
---@alias coinbase.EvmAddressCriterionType "evmAddress"

---The transaction `to` address an `evmAddress` criterion compared. For a token transfer, this is the token contract, not the token recipient; use an `evmData` criterion to constrain the recipient.
---@class coinbase.EvmAddressObservation
