---@class coinbase.EvmCall
---@field to string The address the call is directed to.
---@field value string The amount of ETH to send with the call, in wei.
---@field data string The call data to send. This is the hex-encoded data of the function call consisting of the method selector and the function arguments.
---@field overrideGasLimit? string The override gas limit to use for the call instead of the bundler's estimated gas limit.

---A single condition to apply against the function and encoded arguments in the transaction's `data` field. Each `parameter` configuration must be successfully evaluated against the corresponding function argument in order for a policy to be accepted.
---@class coinbase.EvmDataCondition
---@field ["function"] string The name of a smart contract function being called.
---@field params? coinbase.EvmDataConditionParamsList An optional list of parameter conditions to apply against encoded arguments in the transaction's `data` field.

---A list of parameter conditions to apply against encoded arguments in the transaction's `data` field.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataConditionParamsItem coinbase.EvmDataParameterCondition|coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionList

---An optional list of parameter conditions to apply against encoded arguments in the transaction's `data` field.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataConditionParamsList coinbase.EvmDataConditionParamsItem[]

---A schema for specifying a criterion for the `data` field of an EVM transaction.
---@class coinbase.EvmDataCriterion
---@field type coinbase.EvmDataCriterionType|string The type of criterion to use. This should be `evmData`.
---@field abi coinbase.EvmDataCriterionAbi The ABI of the smart contract being called. This can be a partial structure with only specific functions.
---@field conditions coinbase.EvmDataCriterionConditionsList A list of conditions to apply against the function and encoded arguments in the transaction's `data` field. Each condition must be met in order for this policy to be accepted or rejected.

---The ABI of the smart contract being called. This can be a partial structure with only specific functions.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataCriterionAbi coinbase.KnownAbiType|string|coinbase.Abi

---A list of conditions to apply against the function and encoded arguments in the transaction's `data` field. Each condition must be met in order for this policy to be accepted or rejected.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataCriterionConditionsList coinbase.EvmDataCondition[]

---The type of criterion to use. This should be `evmData`.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataCriterionType "evmData"

---The call an `evmData` criterion decoded from the transaction `data` with the criterion's `abi`. Parameters are checked against the first of the criterion's `conditions` whose `function` equals `function`.
---@class coinbase.EvmDataObservation
---@field type coinbase.EvmDataObservationType The criterion type.
---@field selector? string The 4-byte function selector. Omitted when `data` is shorter than 4 bytes.
---@field ["function"]? string The name of the ABI function with this selector. Omitted when no function in the `abi` has it.
---@field arguments coinbase.EvmDataObservationArgumentsList The decoded arguments of `function`, in ABI order. Empty when `function` is omitted. Only the first 32 arguments are returned.

---The decoded arguments of `function`, in ABI order. Empty when `function` is omitted. Only the first 32 arguments are returned.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataObservationArgumentsList coinbase.ObservedArgument[]

---The criterion type.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataObservationType "evmData"

---@class coinbase.EvmDataParameterCondition
---@field name string The name of the parameter to check against a transaction's calldata. If name is unknown, or is not named, you may supply an array index, e.g., `0` for first parameter.
---@field operator coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionOperator|string The operator to use for the comparison. The value resolved at the `name` will be on the left-hand side of the operator, and the `value` field will be on the right-hand side.
---@field value string A single value to compare the value resolved at `name` to. All values are encoded as strings. Refer to the table in the documentation for how values should be encoded, and which operators are supported for each type.

---@class coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionList
---@field name string The name of the parameter to check against a transaction's calldata. If name is unknown, or is not named, you may supply an array index, e.g., `0` for first parameter.
---@field operator coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionListOperator|string The operator to use for the comparison. The value resolved at the `name` will be on the left-hand side of the operator, and the `values` field will be on the right-hand side.
---@field values coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionListValuesList Values to compare against the resolved `name` value. All values are encoded as strings. Refer to the table in the documentation for how values should be encoded, and which operators are supported for each type.

---The operator to use for the comparison. The value resolved at the `name` will be on the left-hand side of the operator, and the `values` field will be on the right-hand side.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionListOperator "in"|"not in"

---Values to compare against the resolved `name` value. All values are encoded as strings. Refer to the table in the documentation for how values should be encoded, and which operators are supported for each type.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionListValuesList string[]

---The operator to use for the comparison. The value resolved at the `name` will be on the left-hand side of the operator, and the `value` field will be on the right-hand side.
---@alias coinbase.EvmDataParameterConditionOperator ">"|">="|"<"|"<="|"=="

