---The unmet criterion, exactly as defined in the rule, discriminated by `type`.
---@alias coinbase.PolicyCriterion coinbase.EthValueCriterion|coinbase.EvmAddressCriterion|coinbase.EvmNetworkCriterion|coinbase.EvmDataCriterion|coinbase.EvmMessageCriterion|coinbase.SignEvmTypedDataFieldCriterion|coinbase.SignEvmTypedDataVerifyingContractCriterion|coinbase.NetUSDChangeCriterion|coinbase.SolAddressCriterion|coinbase.SolValueCriterion|coinbase.SplAddressCriterion|coinbase.SplValueCriterion|coinbase.MintAddressCriterion|coinbase.SolDataCriterion|coinbase.SolMessageCriterion|coinbase.ProgramIdCriterion|coinbase.SolNetworkCriterion

---The value taken from the operation that a criterion was compared against, discriminated by the criterion's `type`. Amounts use the criterion's units: integer strings of base units (wei, lamports, or token atomic units) and USD in integer cents, so a unit mistake in a rule shows as a difference in magnitude. A field is omitted when the operation has no such value; each field says when that happens.
---Values come only from the request, the prepared user operation it names, transaction simulation, and the rate-limit counters the criterion reads. These are never returned: signatures, raw transaction bytes, calldata or instruction data beyond the decoded selector, instruction and arguments, the operations or accounts that make up a rate-limit total, and simulation results other than the net USD change. A string longer than its `maxLength` is cut to its first `maxLength` characters and marked `truncated: true`.
---@alias coinbase.PolicyCriterionObservation coinbase.EthValueObservation|coinbase.EvmAddressObservation|coinbase.EvmNetworkObservation|coinbase.EvmDataObservation|coinbase.EvmMessageObservation|coinbase.EvmTypedDataFieldObservation|coinbase.EvmTypedDataVerifyingContractObservation|coinbase.NetUSDChangeObservation|coinbase.SolAddressObservation|coinbase.SolValueObservation|coinbase.SplAddressObservation|coinbase.SplValueObservation|coinbase.MintAddressObservation|coinbase.SolDataObservation|coinbase.SolMessageObservation|coinbase.ProgramIdObservation|coinbase.SolNetworkObservation|coinbase.RateLimitingObservation

---A list of rules that comprise the policy. Each policy is limited to 100 rules and a total serialized size of 8 MiB.
---@alias coinbase.PolicyRules coinbase.Rule[]

---The scope of the policy. Only one project-level policy can exist at any time.
---@alias coinbase.PolicyScope "project"|"account"

---The action the real operation would take and why. `matchedRule` is present exactly when `reason` is `rule_accepted` or `rule_rejected`.
---@class coinbase.PolicySimulationResult
---@field action coinbase.PolicySimulationResultAction Whether the real operation would be accepted or rejected.
---@field reason coinbase.PolicySimulationResultReason Why the operation got its `action`. Each value implies exactly one `action`. Within a policy, a matching `reject` rule overrides any matching `accept` rule, regardless of rule order. With `accept`: `rule_accepted` means `matchedRule` matched all of its criteria, its action is `accept`, and no `reject` rule in the same policy matched. `no_rule_for_operation` means no rule targeted the operation, so it was accepted by default. With `reject`: `rule_rejected` means `matchedRule` matched all of its criteria and its action is `reject`, so the rejection is caused by the entire rule. `no_rule_matched` means at least one rule targeted the operation but none matched, so it was rejected by default; `unmatchedRules` shows the criterion that disqualified each one.
---@field matchedRule? coinbase.MatchedPolicyRule
---@field unmatchedRules coinbase.PolicySimulationResultUnmatchedRulesList Rules targeting the operation that were evaluated and did not match. Within a policy, `reject` rules are evaluated before `accept` rules, and evaluation stops at `matchedRule`. Rules that were not evaluated are omitted. When there is no `matchedRule`, every rule that targeted the operation appears here. Among matching rules with the same action, the first in policy order is `matchedRule`.
---@field evaluatedPolicies coinbase.PolicySimulationResultEvaluatedPoliciesList Policies iterated, in order: the project policy, then the account policy. Evaluation stops at the policy containing `matchedRule`. End-user operations consult only the project policy.
---@field evaluatedUnit? coinbase.EvaluatedUnit

---Whether the real operation would be accepted or rejected.
---@alias coinbase.PolicySimulationResultAction "accept"|"reject"

---Policies iterated, in order: the project policy, then the account policy. Evaluation stops at the policy containing `matchedRule`. End-user operations consult only the project policy.
---@alias coinbase.PolicySimulationResultEvaluatedPoliciesList coinbase.EvaluatedPolicy[]

---Why the operation got its `action`. Each value implies exactly one `action`.
---Within a policy, a matching `reject` rule overrides any matching `accept` rule, regardless of rule order.
---With `accept`: `rule_accepted` means `matchedRule` matched all of its criteria, its action is `accept`, and no `reject` rule in the same policy matched. `no_rule_for_operation` means no rule targeted the operation, so it was accepted by default.
---With `reject`: `rule_rejected` means `matchedRule` matched all of its criteria and its action is `reject`, so the rejection is caused by the entire rule. `no_rule_matched` means at least one rule targeted the operation but none matched, so it was rejected by default; `unmatchedRules` shows the criterion that disqualified each one.
---@alias coinbase.PolicySimulationResultReason "rule_accepted"|"rule_rejected"|"no_rule_matched"|"no_rule_for_operation"

---Rules targeting the operation that were evaluated and did not match. Within a policy, `reject` rules are evaluated before `accept` rules, and evaluation stops at `matchedRule`. Rules that were not evaluated are omitted. When there is no `matchedRule`, every rule that targeted the operation appears here. Among matching rules with the same action, the first in policy order is `matchedRule`.
---@alias coinbase.PolicySimulationResultUnmatchedRulesList coinbase.UnmatchedPolicyRule[]

---The current evaluation status of the policy.
---@alias coinbase.PolicyStatus "active"|"paused"

