---Metadata for one Terms of Service document a Customer may need to
---accept. Each entry represents one logical document (identified by
---`versionId`) that may be published in multiple languages —
---`languages` lists the BCP 47 language tags the document is available
---to view and accept in. An optional `deadline` records the end of a grace
---period: a future deadline is non-blocking `due`, an elapsed deadline is
---`past_due`, and no deadline means acceptance is required immediately with
---status `due`. `url` is the canonical, language-agnostic document URL;
---partners append `?lang=<tag>` (where `<tag>` is one of `languages`) to
---retrieve a specific translation, and omit the parameter to let the
---documentation site choose a default. This API does not serve Terms of
---Service body content; this schema describes metadata only.
---@class coinbase.TermsOfService
---@field versionId string Stable identifier for this Terms of Service document. Submit this value as `versionId` on a `TosAcceptance` to record acceptance.
---@field deadline? string Optional deadline by which the Customer must accept this Terms of Service version, in ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 format. A future deadline is non-blocking grace with requirement status `due`; an elapsed deadline produces `past_due`. When omitted, acceptance is required immediately and the requirement status remains `due`.
---@field languages coinbase.TermsOfServiceLanguagesList BCP 47 language tags this Terms of Service document can be viewed and accepted in. The list is non-empty (every published document carries at least one language). Append the chosen tag to `url` as `?lang=<tag>` to fetch the localized document, and submit the same tag as `language` on the corresponding `TosAcceptance` to record which translation the Customer reviewed.
---@field url string Canonical, language-agnostic URL where the Terms of Service document is hosted (for example, `https://www.coinbase.com/legal/user-agreements-third-party-provider`). Append `?lang=<tag>` (where `<tag>` is one of `languages`) to retrieve a specific translation; without the parameter, the documentation site renders a default translation.

---BCP 47 language tags this Terms of Service document can be viewed
---and accepted in. The list is non-empty (every published document
---carries at least one language). Append the chosen tag to `url` as
---`?lang=<tag>` to fetch the localized document, and submit the same
---tag as `language` on the corresponding `TosAcceptance` to record
---which translation the Customer reviewed.
---@alias coinbase.TermsOfServiceLanguagesList string[]

---General information about a token. Includes the type, the network, and other identifying information.
---@class coinbase.Token
---@field network coinbase.ListEvmTokenBalancesNetwork
---@field symbol? string The symbol of this token (ex: SOL, ETH, USDC). The token symbol is not unique. It is possible for two different tokens to have the same symbol. For native gas tokens, this symbol is defined via convention. As an example, for ETH on Ethereum mainnet, the symbol is "ETH". For ERC-20 tokens, this symbol is defined via configuration. `symbol` will be the string returned by `function symbol() public view returns (string)` on the underlying token contract. Not all tokens have a symbol, as this function is [optional in the ERC-20 specification](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-20#symbol). This field will only be populated when the token's underlying ERC-20 contract has a `symbol()` function. Further, this endpoint will only populate this value for a small subset of whitelisted ERC-20 tokens at this time. We intend to improve coverage in the future.
---@field name? string The name of this token (ex: "Solana", "Ether", "USD Coin"). The token name is not unique. It is possible for two different tokens to have the same name. For native gas tokens, this name is defined via convention. As an example, for ETH on Ethereum mainnet, the name is "Ether". For ERC-20 tokens, this name is defined via configuration. `name` will be the string returned by `function name() public view returns (string)` on the underlying token contract. Not all tokens have a name, as this function is [optional in the ERC-20 specification](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-20#name). This field will only be populated when the token's underlying ERC-20 contract has a `name()` function. Further, this endpoint will only populate this value for a small subset of whitelisted ERC-20 tokens at this time. We intend to improve coverage in the future.
---@field contractAddress string The contract address of the token. For Ether, the contract address is `0xEeeeeEeeeEeEeeEeEeEeeEEEeeeeEeeeeeeeEEeE` per [EIP-7528](https://github.com/ethereum/EIPs/blob/master/EIPS/eip-7528.md). For ERC-20 tokens, this is the contract address where the token is deployed.

---Amount of a given token.
---@class coinbase.TokenAmount
---@field amount string The amount is denominated in the smallest indivisible unit of the token. For ETH, the smallest indivisible unit is Wei (10^-18 ETH). For ERC-20s, the smallest unit is the unit returned from `function totalSupply() public view returns (uint256)`.
---@field decimals number 'decimals' is the exponential value N that satisfies the equation `amount * 10^-N = standard_denomination`. The standard denomination is the most commonly used denomination for the token. - In the case of the native gas token, `decimals` is defined via convention. As an example, for ETH of Ethereum mainnet, the standard denomination is 10^-18 the smallest denomination (Wei). As such, for ETH on Ethereum mainnet, `decimals` is 18. - In the case of ERC-20 tokens, `decimals` is defined via configuration. `decimals` will be the number returned by `function decimals() public view returns (uint8)` on the underlying token contract. Not all tokens have a `decimals` field, as this function is [optional in the ERC-20 specification](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-20#decimals). This field will be left empty if the underlying token contract doesn't implement `decimals`. Further, this endpoint will only populate this value for a small subset of whitelisted ERC-20 tokens at this time. We intend to improve coverage in the future.

---@class coinbase.TokenBalance
---@field amount coinbase.TokenAmount
---@field token coinbase.Token

---@class coinbase.TokenFee
---@field amount string The estimated amount of the fee in atomic units of the `token`. For example, `1000000000000000` if the fee is in ETH equates to 0.001 ETH, `10000` if the fee is in USDC equates to 0.01 USDC, etc.
---@field token string The contract address of the token that the fee is paid in. The address `0xEeeeeEeeeEeEeeEeEeEeeEEEeeeeEeeeeeeeEEeE` is used for the native token of the network (e.g. ETH).

---Display details resolved at creation and stored on the immutable Top-Up Link. These details are returned in the create response and creation webhook.
---@class coinbase.TopUpCustomerDisplay
---@field merchantName string The stored merchant name displayed on the hosted Top-Up page. This is the supplied name with surrounding whitespace removed, or the entity's profile name when no nonempty override was supplied. The stored name does not change when the entity's profile changes. The supplied-name length limit does not constrain the profile-name fallback.

---Display details supplied for the hosted Top-Up page. Only the merchant name is supported. Unrecognized fields are allowed and ignored.
---@class coinbase.TopUpCustomerDisplayInput
---@field merchantName? string The merchant name to display on the hosted Top-Up page. The limit counts Unicode code points in the supplied value, including surrounding whitespace. Surrounding whitespace is removed before storage. When omitted or empty after trimming, the entity's profile name is used.

---A shareable link that lets a payer add funds to their balance through a hosted Top-Up flow. The resource is immutable once created. The link expires 24 hours after creation and funds a single purchase: once a purchase succeeds, the link is spent and cannot be used again. A purchase that fails does not consume the link, so the payer can retry until it expires. A link is not bound to a specific payer. `orderTotalAmount` and `redirectUrl` are omitted from the response when they were not supplied at creation; they are never returned as null. `customerDisplay` contains the resolved merchant name stored at creation, including the entity's profile name when no nonempty override was supplied. The response and creation webhook always include `customerDisplay` and its `merchantName`.
---@class coinbase.TopUpLink
---@field topUpLinkId string
---@field topUpAmount any The merchant-provided initial suggested net amount to add for the link's single purchase, denominated in `asset`. The suggestion remains fixed on the link and is not recomputed from `orderTotalAmount` or the payer's current available balance. The payer can adjust the amount they add in the hosted flow. Fiat fees are outside this value.
---@field asset any The asset credited by the Top-Up Link. Currently, only `usdc` is supported.
---@field orderTotalAmount? any The total balance, denominated in `asset`, that the merchant expects the payer to need to complete the order, as supplied at creation. When present, the hosted Top-Up page shows the order total and the payer's current available balance, and computes the remaining shortfall from those values. This live shortfall is separate from `topUpAmount` and does not replace or change that fixed suggestion. It does not limit the amount the payer can add. Omitted when not supplied at creation.
---@field redirectUrl? string The absolute HTTPS URL to which the payer is redirected after the top-up completes, as supplied at creation. Omitted when not supplied at creation. This value can contain sensitive merchant parameters; treat it as secret and do not log it.
---@field customerDisplay coinbase.TopUpCustomerDisplay
---@field topUpUrl string The hosted Top-Up page URL. Share this URL only with the intended payer. The URL identifies the Top-Up Link but does not authorize a purchase; the payer must authenticate and approve the purchase.
---@field expiresAt string The UTC ISO 8601 timestamp after which the link can no longer be used, 24 hours after creation. A link that has already funded a purchase is spent before this time.
---@field createdAt string The UTC ISO 8601 timestamp at which the Top-Up Link was created.

---A single Terms of Service acceptance recorded for a Customer. Submit
---one entry per required document listed in
---`Customer.requirements.tos.tosVersions[]` (returned on `Get Customer`,
---`Create Customer`, and `Update Customer`). `language` records the
---single translation the Customer actually reviewed.
---
---When new required Terms of Service versions are published, only the
---new `versionId`s appear in `Customer.requirements.tos.tosVersions[]`;
---submit acceptances for only those new version(s).
---@class coinbase.TosAcceptance
---@field versionId string The `versionId` of the Terms of Service document being accepted, as listed in `Customer.requirements.tos.tosVersions[]`.
---@field language string BCP 47 language tag of the Terms of Service translation the Customer reviewed. At write time the server rejects values that are not listed under `languages` on the matching required document for this Customer (same `versionId` as listed in `Customer.requirements.tos.tosVersions[]`).
---@field acceptedAt string Timestamp at which the Customer accepted the Terms of Service, in ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 format. The server may validate or reject obviously non-credible timestamps; when enforcement tightens, the authoritative acceptance time may be recorded server-side instead of trusting client-supplied values alone.

---A Transfer represents all the information needed to execute a transfer and tracks the lifecycle of a transfer from initiation through completion or failure.
---@class coinbase.Transfer
---@field transferId? string The ID of the transfer. Required when validateOnly is false.
---@field status? coinbase.TransferStatus
---@field source coinbase.TransferSource
---@field target coinbase.TransferTarget
---@field sourceAmount? string The amount of the source asset that will be transferred out, as a decimal string in standard unit denomination.
---@field sourceAsset? string The asset symbol of the source amount.
---@field targetAmount? string The amount of the target asset received, as a decimal string in standard unit denomination. May be omitted in the `quoted` state if the value cannot be guaranteed; see `estimate.targetAmount` for the expected value. Populated with the actual executed amount once the transfer completes.
---@field targetAsset? string The asset symbol of the target amount.
---@field exchangeRate? coinbase.TransferExchangeRate Exchange rate information for currency conversion. The rate indicates how much of the target asset is equivalent to one unit of the source asset. May be omitted in the `quoted` state if the rate cannot be guaranteed; see `estimate.exchangeRate` for the expected rate. Populated with the actual executed rate once the transfer completes.
---@field fees? coinbase.TransferFees The fees associated with this transfer. Different transfer types have different fee structures. May be omitted in the `quoted` state if the fees cannot be guaranteed; see `estimate.fees` for the expected fees. Populated with the actual fees once the transfer completes.
---@field estimate? coinbase.TransferEstimate
---@field completedAt? string The date and time the transfer was completed.
---@field failureReason? string The reason for failure, if the transfer failed. Only present when status is `failed`.
---@field expiresAt? string The date and time when this transfer will expire if not executed. Only present for `quoted` status. A new transfer must be created to obtain an updated quote after expiration. Required when validateOnly is false.
---@field executedAt? string The date and time the transfer was executed and moved to processing. Only present when status has progressed beyond `quoted`.
---@field createdAt? string The date and time the transfer was created. Required when validateOnly is false.
---@field updatedAt? string The date and time the transfer was last updated. Required when validateOnly is false.
---@field metadata? coinbase.Metadata
---@field details? coinbase.TransferDetails

---Additional details about the transfer. For example, if the transfer was sent to a deposit destination, the information about that destination will be included in this field.
---@class coinbase.TransferDetails
---@field depositDestination? coinbase.DepositDestinationReference
---@field onchainTransactions? coinbase.TransferDetailsOnchainTransactionsList The onchain transactions associated with the transfer.
---@field travelRule? coinbase.TransferDetailsTravelRule Travel rule compliance status for deposit transfers. Present when the transfer requires travel rule information.

---An onchain transaction associated with the transfer.
---@class coinbase.TransferDetailsOnchainTransactionsItem
---@field transactionHash string The transaction hash.
---@field network coinbase.PaymentNetwork

---The onchain transactions associated with the transfer.
---@alias coinbase.TransferDetailsOnchainTransactionsList coinbase.TransferDetailsOnchainTransactionsItem[]

---Travel rule compliance status for deposit transfers. Present when the transfer requires travel rule information.
---@class coinbase.TransferDetailsTravelRule
---@field status? coinbase.TravelRuleStatus
---@field statusMessage? string Additional details about the current travel rule status. For example, when status is `incomplete`, this may indicate the specific missing information required to proceed.

---Captures estimated values for transfers where amounts can't be guaranteed (e.g., USDC -> EURC).
---
---The values in `estimate` are not modified after a transfer is executed. They are preserved as an immutable record of the original pre-execution snapshot.
---
---The actual executed values are populated in the `transfer` resource post-execution.
---@class coinbase.TransferEstimate
---@field exchangeRate? coinbase.TransferExchangeRate The estimated exchange rate at the time this estimate was captured.
---@field targetAmount? string Estimated amount of the target asset that will be received, as a decimal string in standard unit denomination.
---@field targetAsset? string The asset symbol of the estimated target amount.
---@field fees? coinbase.TransferFees The estimated fees at the time this estimate was captured.
---@field estimatedAt string The date and time when this estimate was captured.

---Exchange rate information for currency conversion. The rate indicates how much of the target asset is equivalent to one unit of the source asset.
---@class coinbase.TransferExchangeRate
---@field sourceAsset string The asset being converted from.
---@field targetAsset string The asset being converted to.
---@field rate string The exchange rate value as a decimal string. Indicates how many units of the target asset equal one unit of the source asset.

---A single fee for a transfer.
---@class coinbase.TransferFee
---@field type coinbase.TransferFeeType The type of the fee, indicating its purpose.
---@field amount string The amount of the fee in units of the asset specified by `asset`.
---@field asset string The asset symbol.

---The type of the fee, indicating its purpose.
---@alias coinbase.TransferFeeType "bank"|"conversion"|"network"|"other"

---The fees associated with this transfer. Different transfer types have different fee structures.
---
---**NOTE:** These examples are not exhaustive.
---
---Common examples:
---* **Crypto transfers**: Network fees (gas) paid in the native token
---* **Fiat conversions**: Processing fees + exchange fees in USD
---* **Wire transfers**: Wire fees ($15) + processing fees ($5) in USD
---* **Crypto conversions**: Spread fees paid in the source asset.
---@alias coinbase.TransferFees coinbase.TransferFee[]

---The source of the transfer.
---@alias coinbase.TransferSource coinbase.TransfersAccount|coinbase.PaymentMethod|coinbase.OnchainAddress|coinbase.AchDepositSource|coinbase.FedwireDepositSource

---The current status of the transfer, indicating what action you need to take next. Required when validateOnly is false.
---@alias coinbase.TransferStatus "quoted"|"processing"|"completed"|"failed"

---The target of the transfer.
---@alias coinbase.TransferTarget coinbase.TransfersAccount|coinbase.PaymentMethod|coinbase.OnchainAddress|coinbase.EmailInstrument

---The Account specific details for the transfer.
---@class coinbase.TransfersAccount
---@field accountId string The ID of the Account.
---@field asset string The asset symbol. Supported values are `usdc`, `eurc`, `usd`, and `eur`.

