---Immutable configuration for an x402 batch-settlement payment channel. The EIP-712 hash of this struct produces the `channelId` used by all batch-settlement payloads.
---@class coinbase.X402BatchSettlementChannelConfig
---@field payer string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the payer (channel funder).
---@field payerAuthorizer string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address authorized to sign vouchers on behalf of the payer.
---@field receiver string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the receiver (resource server / merchant).
---@field receiverAuthorizer string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address authorized to sign claim batches on behalf of the receiver (typically the facilitator).
---@field token string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the ERC-20 payment token.
---@field withdrawDelay number The non-cooperative withdraw delay in seconds. Must be between 900 (15 minutes) and 2,592,000 (30 days).
---@field salt string A 32-byte salt used to differentiate channels between the same payer/receiver pair.

---A single voucher claim within a batched on-chain claim transaction. Used by `x402BatchSettlementClaimPayload.claims` and by the server-enriched shape of `x402BatchSettlementRefundPayload.claims`.
---NOTE: the nested `voucher` here has a **different shape** from the top-level `x402BatchSettlementVoucher` schema. The top-level voucher is the signed cumulative-ceiling message sent by a client (`{channelId, maxClaimableAmount, signature}`). This nested `voucher` mirrors the on-chain claim struct (`{channel: ChannelConfig, maxClaimableAmount}`) that participates in the EIP-712 hash, with `signature` and `totalClaimed` as siblings rather than nested fields. The field names match the upstream x402 protocol and the on-chain Solidity struct; they cannot be renamed without breaking wire and EIP-712 compatibility.
---@class coinbase.X402BatchSettlementClaim
---@field voucher coinbase.X402BatchSettlementClaimVoucher The voucher to claim, identified by the channel config it was signed against and its cumulative ceiling. Field shape mirrors the on-chain claim struct.
---@field signature string The voucher signature from `payerAuthorizer`.
---@field totalClaimed string The cumulative amount already claimed from this channel as of this claim.

---Server-to-facilitator request to batch on-chain claims of accumulated vouchers. `claimAuthorizerSignature` is optional; when absent the facilitator auto-signs with its receiver-authorizer key.
---@class coinbase.X402BatchSettlementClaimPayload
---@field type coinbase.X402BatchSettlementClaimPayloadType|string The payload-type discriminator. Must be `"claim"` for a server-to-facilitator on-chain claim batch request.
---@field claims coinbase.X402BatchSettlementClaimPayloadClaimsList The list of voucher claims to batch in a single on-chain `claim` call.
---@field claimAuthorizerSignature? string Optional EIP-712 signature from the receiver authorizer over the claim batch. When omitted, the facilitator auto-signs.

---The list of voucher claims to batch in a single on-chain `claim` call.
---@alias coinbase.X402BatchSettlementClaimPayloadClaimsList coinbase.X402BatchSettlementClaim[]

