---A single discovered x402 resource. Its fields come from three sources:
---
---- **x402 protocol** — negotiated from the resource's payment-required response: `resource`,
---  `type`, `x402Version`, `accepts`, `extensions`.
---- **Provider-supplied** — metadata published by the resource owner: `description`,
---  `serviceName`, `tags`.
---- **Coinbase-derived** — added during ingestion and curation: `iconUrl`, `quality`,
---  `lastUpdated`, and (for Coinbase-curated endpoints only) `curated`, `skillUrl` (a
---  Coinbase-authored SKILL.md), and `bundleSlugs`.
---@class coinbase.X402DiscoveryResource
---@field resource string The URL of the resource.
---@field description? string A human-readable description of the resource.
---@field type coinbase.X402DiscoveryResourceType Communication protocol (e.g., "http", "mcp").
---@field x402Version coinbase.X402Version
---@field lastUpdated? string Timestamp of the last update.
---@field accepts? coinbase.X402DiscoveryResourceAcceptsList Payment requirements accepted by the resource.
---@field extensions? coinbase.X402DiscoveryResourceExtensionsMap Map of x402 protocol extensions supported by the resource, keyed by extension name.
---@field quality? coinbase.X402ResourceQuality
---@field serviceName? string Display name of the service this resource belongs to. This is a free-form label for grouping and presentation only — it is not a stable identifier, and two resources sharing the same `serviceName` are not guaranteed to belong to the same logical service.
---@field tags? coinbase.X402DiscoveryResourceTagsList Low-cardinality string labels associated with the resource for client-side filtering and display. Values are free-form (no controlled vocabulary) and case-sensitive. Order is not significant and duplicates are not expected.
---@field bundleSlugs? coinbase.X402DiscoveryResourceBundleSlugsList Slugs of the curated x402 bundles this resource belongs to. A bundle is an ordered, named grouping of curated resources covering a common agent workflow. Present only for Coinbase-curated resources (`curated: true`); omitted when the resource is not curated or is not a member of any bundle.
---@field iconUrl? string URL of a square icon representing the service this resource belongs to. Distinct from a brand logo: this is intended for compact, list-view rendering (favicon-style) and is normalized to a square aspect ratio at ingestion. The image is moderated and re-hosted by Coinbase, so the URL is stable and safe to render directly in clients. Omitted when the provider did not supply an icon, when the supplied icon failed moderation, or when image processing was unavailable at ingestion time.
---@field curated? boolean Whether this resource is a Coinbase-curated endpoint. Curated endpoints have passed the partner-admission and verification bar and surface higher in search and listing results. Omitted (treated as `false`) when the resource is not curated.
---@field skillUrl? string URL of the SKILL.md document describing how to use this resource. Omitted when the resource has no associated skill document.

