---The supported payment kind for the x402 protocol. A kind is comprised of a scheme and a network, which together uniquely identify a way to move money on the x402 protocol. For more details, please see [x402 Schemes](https://github.com/coinbase/x402?tab=readme-ov-file#schemes).
---@class coinbase.X402SupportedPaymentKind
---@field x402Version coinbase.X402Version
---@field scheme coinbase.X402SupportedPaymentKindScheme The scheme of the payment protocol.
---@field network coinbase.X402SupportedPaymentKindNetwork The network of the blockchain. The format corresponds to the `x402Version` of the enclosing `x402SupportedPaymentKind`: v1 uses human-readable names (see `X402V1Network`); v2 uses CAIP-2 chain IDs (see `X402V2Network`).
---@field extra? coinbase.X402SupportedPaymentKindExtraMap The optional additional scheme-specific payment info. Common scheme-specific fields: - `exact` on Solana: `feePayer` — the base58-encoded Solana address that pays transaction fees. - `upto` on EVM: `name`, `version`, and `facilitatorAddress` — the EVM address of the facilitator that the client must bind into the Permit2 witness when constructing the payment payload. - `batch-settlement` on EVM: `name`, `version`, `receiverAuthorizer` (the EVM address authorized to sign claim batches), `withdrawDelay` (channel non-cooperative withdraw delay in seconds, 900–2,592,000), and optionally `assetTransferMethod` (e.g., `"eip3009"`).

---The optional additional scheme-specific payment info.
---Common scheme-specific fields:
---  - `exact` on Solana: `feePayer` — the base58-encoded Solana address that pays transaction fees.
---  - `upto` on EVM: `name`, `version`, and `facilitatorAddress` — the EVM address of the facilitator that the client must bind into the Permit2 witness when constructing the payment payload.
---  - `batch-settlement` on EVM: `name`, `version`, `receiverAuthorizer` (the EVM address authorized to sign claim batches), `withdrawDelay` (channel non-cooperative withdraw delay in seconds, 900–2,592,000), and optionally `assetTransferMethod` (e.g., `"eip3009"`).
---@alias coinbase.X402SupportedPaymentKindExtraMap { [string]: any }

---The network of the blockchain. The format corresponds to the `x402Version` of the enclosing `x402SupportedPaymentKind`: v1 uses human-readable names (see `X402V1Network`); v2 uses CAIP-2 chain IDs (see `X402V2Network`).
---@alias coinbase.X402SupportedPaymentKindNetwork "base-sepolia"|"base"|"solana-devnet"|"solana"|"eip155:8453"|"eip155:84532"|"eip155:137"|"eip155:42161"|"eip155:143"|"eip155:480"|"eip155:4801"|"solana:5eykt4UsFv8P8NJdTREpY1vzqKqZKvdp"|"solana:EtWTRABZaYq6iMfeYKouRu166VU2xqa1"

---The scheme of the payment protocol.
---@alias coinbase.X402SupportedPaymentKindScheme "exact"|"upto"|"batch-settlement"

---The x402 protocol upto scheme payload for EVM networks using Permit2. The `upto` scheme authorizes a maximum amount and lets the facilitator settle for the actual amount used. Structurally identical to `x402ExactEvmPermit2Payload` except `permit2Authorization.witness` carries an additional `facilitator` address that binds the authorization to a specific facilitator (the one announced via `extra.facilitatorAddress` in the payment requirements). For more details, see [EVM Upto Scheme Details](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/blob/main/specs/schemes/upto/scheme_upto_evm.md).
---@class coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2Payload
---@field signature string The EIP-712 hex-encoded signature of the Permit2 PermitWitnessTransferFrom message. Smart account signatures may be longer than 65 bytes.
---@field permit2Authorization coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2PayloadPermit2Authorization The authorization data for the Permit2 PermitWitnessTransferFrom message. The `permitted.amount` is the maximum the client authorizes; the actual settled amount is decided by the resource server at settle time and MUST be less than or equal to it.

---The authorization data for the Permit2 PermitWitnessTransferFrom message. The `permitted.amount` is the maximum the client authorizes; the actual settled amount is decided by the resource server at settle time and MUST be less than or equal to it.
---@class coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2PayloadPermit2Authorization
---@field from string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the sender of the payment.
---@field permitted coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2PayloadPermit2AuthorizationPermitted The token permissions for the transfer.
---@field spender string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the spender (the x402 Upto Permit2 proxy contract).
---@field nonce string The Permit2 nonce as a decimal string (uint256).
---@field deadline string The unix timestamp before which the permit is valid.
---@field witness coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2PayloadPermit2AuthorizationWitness The witness data containing payment details. Includes a `facilitator` field to bind the authorization to a specific facilitator address.

---The token permissions for the transfer.
---@class coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2PayloadPermit2AuthorizationPermitted
---@field token string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the token to transfer.
---@field amount string The maximum amount the client authorizes to transfer in atomic units.

---The witness data containing payment details. Includes a `facilitator` field to bind the authorization to a specific facilitator address.
---@class coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2PayloadPermit2AuthorizationWitness
---@field to string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the recipient.
---@field facilitator string The 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address of the facilitator authorized to settle this payment. MUST match the `facilitatorAddress` advertised in the payment requirements `extra` field.
---@field validAfter string The unix timestamp after which the payment is valid.

---The x402 v1 network identifier. x402 v1 uses human-readable network names. Supported networks: Base mainnet and testnet, Solana mainnet and devnet.
---@alias coinbase.X402V1Network "base"|"base-sepolia"|"solana"|"solana-devnet"

---The x402 v1 protocol payment payload. Uses human-readable network names and requires `scheme` and `network` alongside the inner `payload` object.
---@class coinbase.X402V1PaymentPayload
---@field x402Version coinbase.X402Version|number The x402 protocol version. Must be `1` for this payload shape.
---@field scheme coinbase.X402V1PaymentPayloadScheme|string The scheme of the payment protocol to use. Currently, the only supported scheme is `exact`.
---@field network coinbase.X402V1Network|string The network of the blockchain to send payment on.
---@field payload coinbase.X402V1PaymentPayloadPayload The payload of the payment depending on the x402Version, scheme, and network.

---The payload of the payment depending on the x402Version, scheme, and network.
---@alias coinbase.X402V1PaymentPayloadPayload coinbase.X402ExactEvmPayload|coinbase.X402ExactEvmPermit2Payload|coinbase.X402ExactSolanaPayload

---The scheme of the payment protocol to use. Currently, the only supported scheme is `exact`.
---@alias coinbase.X402V1PaymentPayloadScheme "exact"

---The x402 v1 payment requirements. Uses human-readable network names, and carries resource metadata (`resource`, `description`, `mimeType`) alongside the payment fields. The only supported scheme is `exact`.
---@class coinbase.X402V1PaymentRequirements
---@field scheme coinbase.X402V1PaymentRequirementsScheme|string The scheme of the payment protocol to use. Currently, the only supported scheme is `exact`.
---@field network coinbase.X402V1Network|string The network of the blockchain to send payment on.
---@field maxAmountRequired string The maximum amount required to pay for the resource in atomic units of the payment asset.
---@field resource string The URL of the resource to pay for.
---@field description string A human-readable description of the resource.
---@field mimeType string The MIME type of the resource response.
---@field outputSchema? coinbase.X402V1PaymentRequirementsOutputSchemaMap The optional JSON schema describing the resource output.
---@field payTo string The destination to pay value to. For EVM networks, payTo will be a 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address. For Solana-based networks, payTo will be a base58-encoded Solana address.
---@field maxTimeoutSeconds number The maximum time in seconds for the resource server to respond.
---@field asset string The asset to pay with. For EVM networks, the asset will be a 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address. For Solana-based networks, the asset will be a base58-encoded Solana address.
---@field extra? coinbase.X402V1PaymentRequirementsExtraMap The optional additional scheme-specific payment info.

---The optional additional scheme-specific payment info.
---@alias coinbase.X402V1PaymentRequirementsExtraMap { [string]: any }

---The optional JSON schema describing the resource output.
---@alias coinbase.X402V1PaymentRequirementsOutputSchemaMap { [string]: any }

---The scheme of the payment protocol to use. Currently, the only supported scheme is `exact`.
---@alias coinbase.X402V1PaymentRequirementsScheme "exact"

---The x402 v2 network identifier in CAIP-2 format. x402 v2 identifies networks by their CAIP-2 chain ID (e.g. `eip155:<chainId>` for EVM networks, `solana:<genesisHash>` for Solana). Supported networks: Base, Polygon, Arbitrum One, World Chain (EVM), Monad (EVM), and Solana.
---@alias coinbase.X402V2Network "eip155:8453"|"eip155:84532"|"eip155:137"|"eip155:42161"|"eip155:143"|"eip155:480"|"eip155:4801"|"solana:5eykt4UsFv8P8NJdTREpY1vzqKqZKvdp"|"solana:EtWTRABZaYq6iMfeYKouRu166VU2xqa1"

---The x402 v2 protocol payment payload. Uses CAIP-2 network identifiers. The `accepted` field carries the full payment requirements; `scheme` and `network` are not top-level fields (they are on the nested `accepted` object).
---@class coinbase.X402V2PaymentPayload
---@field x402Version coinbase.X402Version|number The x402 protocol version. Must be `2` for this payload shape.
---@field payload coinbase.X402V2PaymentPayloadPayload The payload of the payment depending on the x402Version, scheme, and network. Discriminated by scheme-specific fields: exact-EVM/upto-EVM payloads carry a `signature`; exact-Solana carries a `transaction`; batch-settlement carries a `type` discriminator. See `x402BatchSettlementEvmPayload` for the documented batch-settlement variants.
---@field accepted coinbase.X402V2PaymentRequirements
---@field resource? coinbase.X402ResourceInfo
---@field extensions? coinbase.X402V2PaymentPayloadExtensionsMap Optional protocol extensions.

---Optional protocol extensions.
---@alias coinbase.X402V2PaymentPayloadExtensionsMap { [string]: any }

---The payload of the payment depending on the x402Version, scheme, and network. Discriminated by scheme-specific fields: exact-EVM/upto-EVM payloads carry a `signature`; exact-Solana carries a `transaction`; batch-settlement carries a `type` discriminator. See `x402BatchSettlementEvmPayload` for the documented batch-settlement variants.
---@alias coinbase.X402V2PaymentPayloadPayload coinbase.X402ExactEvmPayload|coinbase.X402ExactEvmPermit2Payload|coinbase.X402ExactSolanaPayload|coinbase.X402UptoEvmPermit2Payload|coinbase.X402BatchSettlementEvmPayload

---The x402 v2 payment requirements. Uses CAIP-2 network identifiers and supports `exact`, `upto`, and `batch-settlement` schemes. Carries only the payment fields (no resource metadata — that is in the enclosing `x402V2PaymentPayload.resource`).
---@class coinbase.X402V2PaymentRequirements
---@field scheme coinbase.X402V2PaymentRequirementsScheme|string The scheme of the payment protocol to use. Supported schemes are `exact`, `upto`, and `batch-settlement`.
---@field network coinbase.X402V2Network|string The network of the blockchain to send payment on in CAIP-2 format.
---@field asset string The asset to pay with. For EVM networks, the asset will be a 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address. For Solana-based networks, the asset will be a base58-encoded Solana address.
---@field amount string The amount to pay for the resource in atomic units of the payment asset.
---@field payTo string The destination to pay value to. For EVM networks, payTo will be a 0x-prefixed, checksum EVM address. For Solana-based networks, payTo will be a base58-encoded Solana address.
---@field maxTimeoutSeconds number The maximum time in seconds for the resource server to respond.
---@field extra? coinbase.X402V2PaymentRequirementsExtraMap The optional additional scheme-specific payment info.

---The optional additional scheme-specific payment info.
---@alias coinbase.X402V2PaymentRequirementsExtraMap { [string]: any }

---The scheme of the payment protocol to use. Supported schemes are `exact`, `upto`, and `batch-settlement`.
---@alias coinbase.X402V2PaymentRequirementsScheme "exact"|"upto"|"batch-settlement"

---The result of a single preflight check performed against the x402 endpoint.
---@class coinbase.X402ValidateCheck
---@field check coinbase.X402ValidateCheckCheck The name of the preflight check. New values may be added in future versions; clients should handle unknown values gracefully.
---@field passed boolean Whether the check passed.
---@field detail string A human-readable explanation of the check result.
---@field expected? string The value the check expected, when applicable.
---@field actual? string The value the check observed, when applicable.
---@field severity coinbase.X402ValidateCheckSeverity Whether this check is a hard indexing requirement or a quality recommendation. A `required` check affects validity when it fails. An `advisory` check (for example, a missing output schema) is a suggestion to improve discoverability and does not make the endpoint invalid.

---The name of the preflight check. New values may be added in future versions; clients should handle unknown values gracefully.
---@alias coinbase.X402ValidateCheckCheck "reachable"|"returns_402"|"has_bazaar_extension"|"parse"

---Whether this check is a hard indexing requirement or a quality recommendation. A `required` check affects validity when it fails. An `advisory` check (for example, a missing output schema) is a suggestion to improve discoverability and does not make the endpoint invalid.
---@alias coinbase.X402ValidateCheckSeverity "required"|"advisory"

---Bazaar index status for a validated x402 endpoint.
---@class coinbase.X402ValidateIndex
---@field active boolean Whether the indexed resource is active and served in discovery results.
---@field lastCrawledAt string|distilled.Null When the endpoint was last crawled, or `null` if it has been indexed but not yet crawled.
---@field quality? coinbase.X402ResourceQuality Quality metrics for the indexed resource, present only when the endpoint has call history.

---Response from validating an x402 endpoint's bazaar-discovery configuration.
---@class coinbase.X402ValidateResponse
---@field valid boolean Whether the endpoint is valid: all preflight checks passed and the facilitator would index the resource.
---@field statusCode number|distilled.Null The HTTP status code returned by the endpoint, or `null` if the endpoint was not reachable.
---@field x402Version number|distilled.Null The x402 protocol version advertised by the endpoint, or `null` if it could not be determined. Intentionally a bare integer rather than the `X402Version` enum so the validator can surface unsupported or malformed version values returned by non-conforming endpoints.
---@field preflight coinbase.X402ValidateResponsePreflightList All check results in run order. Well-known check names are `reachable`, `returns_402`, `has_bazaar_extension`, and `parse`. Additional checks may be added in future versions.
---@field paymentRequirements coinbase.X402PaymentRequirements|distilled.Null The raw decoded payment requirements returned by the endpoint, or `null` if the endpoint was not reachable or did not return a parseable 402 payload. Lets sellers inspect exactly what their endpoint is advertising.
---@field bazaarExtension coinbase.X402ValidateResponseBazaarExtensionMap|distilled.Null The `extensions.bazaar` block from the endpoint's discovery metadata, or `null` if the bazaar extension was absent or the endpoint was not reachable. Lets sellers verify the discovery configuration their endpoint is advertising.
---@field simulation coinbase.X402ValidateSimulation
---@field index coinbase.X402ValidateIndex|distilled.Null Bazaar index status for the endpoint, or `null` if the endpoint is not yet indexed. Present on every response regardless of simulation outcome.

