---Create a Top-Up Link
---
---Creates a Top-Up Link: a shareable hosted URL that lets a payer add funds to their balance. The resource is immutable once created. The link expires 24 hours after creation and funds a single purchase: once a purchase succeeds, the link is spent and cannot be used again. A purchase that fails does not consume the link, so the payer can retry until it expires. A link is not bound to a specific payer.
---
---Provide `topUpAmount` and `asset`; `orderTotalAmount`, `redirectUrl`, and `customerDisplay` are optional. When `redirectUrl` is supplied, its origin must exactly match one of the entity's configured allowed origins, and the URL must not contain a percent-decoded query key exactly equal to `toppedUpAmount`. The response includes the hosted `topUpUrl` to share with the payer. Creating a link is signaled to webhook subscribers by the `acceptance.top_up_link.created` event, and the purchase that spends the link emits an `acceptance.top_up_link.funds_added` event.
---
---Supply `customerDisplay.merchantName` to override the merchant name on this link's hosted page. The supplied value must not exceed 128 Unicode code points, including surrounding whitespace. Surrounding whitespace is removed before storage. An omitted or empty name after trimming uses the entity's profile name. The create response and creation webhook always return the resolved name stored on the link.
---
---`POST /v2/top-up-links`
---@param input coinbase.CreateTopUpLinkRequest
---@return coinbase.TopUpLink? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_top_up_link(input) end

---Create transfer
---
---Create a new transfer to move funds from a source to a target.
---All transfers first transition to `quoted`. If `execute: false`, the transfer stays quoted until you call `/v2/transfers/{transferId}/execute`.
---If `execute: true`, quoted status emits momentarily before the transfer moves to `processing`, where execution proceeds. Subscribe to the transfers webhook to  follow progress in real time instead of polling.
---
---`POST /v2/transfers`
---@param input coinbase.CreateTransferRequest
---@return coinbase.Transfer? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_transfer(input) end

---Create webhook subscription
---
---Subscribe to real-time events across CDP products. A webhook subscription provides a `targetURL` and other relevant endpoint configuration to enable receiving webhooks when events occur.
---
---An entity can have up to 100 webhook subscriptions. Once this limit is reached, new webhook subscription creation requests return a `400` error with `errorType: subscription_limit_exceeded`.
---
---### Webhook Signature Verification
---
---All webhooks include an HMAC-SHA256 signed header for security. The signature is signed with the secret that is returned in the `secret` field when creating a subscription.
---
---Do not lose the secret, as you will not be able to recreate it. If you lose the secret, you will need to create a new subscription.
---
---See the [verification guide](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/onramp-&-offramp/webhooks#webhook-signature-verification) for implementation details.
---
---`POST /v2/data/webhooks/subscriptions`
---@param input coinbase.CreateWebhookSubscriptionRequest
---@return coinbase.WebhookSubscriptionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_webhook_subscription(input) end

